On Tue, Apr 01, 2003 at 02:34:21PM -0500, George France wrote:
> Hello Alvin,
> 
> As part of my work at HP, I have been working on the update 2.4.18-27 kernel 
> for RedHat 7.2 on the Alpha Architecture.  Currently my efforts have been 
> redirected within HP and the kernel has been put on the back burner.  

You can find some binary rpms for Alpha kernels which are based
on 2.4.18-27 at
  ftp://ftp.harddata.com/pub/hddcs/3.2/2003-spring/RPMS/alpha/
Source rpms are also around.  This is tested only on my machine
and I really do not know how this will behave under Alvin's loads
but if you want to try then by all means ...

Support for bproc clustering does not harm anything if you are
not using it and do not load 'broc' kernel module which is using
these hooks.

Keep in mind that these kernel need few user space updates
(modutils, iptables, things of that sort) which will still work
with older kernels.

   Michal




