On alpha.crl.dec.com:/pub/linux/people/france/kernel-2.4.18 via ftp you will 
find the kernel bits that we have been working upon at HP.  If you would like 
to test these bits at your own risk,  it would be helpful.  

Any additional rpms that are needed to resolve any dependencies are in the 
updates directory.  The kernel rpms will not update your /etc/aboot.conf, so 
please manually check this file after installing the new rpms and make any 
needed corrections by hand before rebooting your system.

Although the testing so far has been rather extensive, these bits have only 
been tested on a handful of system, so please proceed carefully.

I hope this helps.

Best Regards,


--George



