There is not a list of know problems with kernel.org kernels that we have fix 
in the HP kernel except in Jay's and my head.  We should probably make a 
list.  Let me see, the big ones are:

1) systems with 2G+ and 4G+ DRAM.  There are different issues at the different 
threshholds.
2) systems with multiple pci buses.
3) NUMA.
4) QLogic 1020 and 1040 SCSI cards.
5) Tulip chipsets.
6) The symbios drivers.
7) system lockups under high load.
8) unofficial support of legacy systems. 
9) DAC960 support

We have been working to get many of our patches into 2.4.22 and 2.5.x but some 
fixes like for the tulip chipsets and the QLogic boards will probably never 
be in the kernel.org kernels, as the code is just not acceptable.  I hope 
that 2.4.22 will be much better for most Alpha systems.

Best Regards,


--George


