The RH kernel has the magjc bits for the 'tulip' chipset for x86 and alpha, 
the kernel.org kernel does not.  The de4x5 driver is good but only works well 
in half duplex mode.

> > 6) The symbios drivers.
>
> Could you expand?  Recently I have seen complaints from somebody
> with NCR810a controller and 'sym53c8xx_2' driver but otherwise
> this seems to have quite good record.  I am using this driver myself
> for a very long time.


On systems with either 2G or 4G plus memory, I do not remember which, the 
actual DRAM overlaps the window that was being used for DMA.

I hope this helps.

--George






