Did you look for any labels on the power supply?  It should have some
specifications for input and output requirements.  If not, you can do
a rough estimate:

A 600W power supply will most likely draw about 800VA at full output.
With a 120V input, that's about 7A for continuous operations.  To allow
short term surges but protect against exceptional events, I would use
a 10A fuse.

Note:  there is no warranty at all in the above extimate.  I would
check the label on the power supply first.

