First question - are you supplied with 120 VAC or 240 VAC? Is PS
switched to the correct voltage?

Second - a 600 watt PS when fully loaded needs 600 divided by 120
equals 5 amps ( or for 240 VAC needs 2.5 amps ) so any smaller
fuse isn't "a little low" it is wrong.

Third PS will take a surge on startup this should be accomodated
by using a "SLOW BLOW" fuse not by increasing the steady rating.

As long as you are watching (to put out the fire) it can't hurt
to try a 10 amp fuse. If there is a major problem it will blow
anyway but it would be best to use the smallest fuse that doesn't
blow on powerup consistent with allowing 600 watts to pass.

Somewhere on the PS there should be an Underwriters Laboratory
label which states the maximum current taken.

Stephen Lewis




