Hi,
	I am completely new to Dec Alphas (only owned one two days, so please
excuse these basic questions). 

I have a Dec Personal Workstatation 600a, on which I'm trying to
install Tru64 UNIX. The machine is fitted with a graphics card which
is a 4D51T-2200 PCI Intergraph Powerstorm Intense 3D. I have switched
from AlphaBIOS to SRM but have a few issues mainly related to the
video display, most of which happening even before I load any
operating system. I'm using a Iiyama AUD8431D 19" TFT screen. 

1) The card has two VGA connectors on it - one black, one blue. Why?
Only one (blue) seems to work.

2) When the machine is first powered up, it looks like there are a few
initial messages to the screen which I can't get time to read,
suggesting these appear before the monitor has chance to sync.
Annoying to say the least, as perhaps these are important. Is this
normal ??

3) If the machine is powered up, and just in SRM or even with Tru64
running, removing the monitor cable for a second obviously makes the
monitor go blank - my monitor is not telepathic! However, if I then
re-connect the VGA cable to the graphics card, the monitor always says
"no signal on analog input". Hence swapping the monitor around seems
impossible. I seem able swap the monitor between my main computer (a
Sun) and PC's with no problems, but once removed from the Dec Alphas'
video connector, I have no hope of ever seeing a display again unless
I reset the machine. Is this normal??

4) The card remains in 640x480 at all times - even when Tru64 is
running. This seems a bit odd. 

5) I had a problem with a dodgy SCSI disk. Some error messages were
generated in SRM console, but these scrolled off the screen. Is there
any way to prevent this - i.e. effectively pipe them to 'more' or some
other method?

6) It looks to me like some things (floppy contoller enbable/disable,
perhaps cache) can only be accessed via the AlphaBIOS setup program.
While I switched from AlphaBIOS to SRM in the AlphaBIOS setup program
(bit like a nomal PC bios), how could I switch back to AlphaBIOS if I
wanted to?







