Dear John & list,

Below is good advice and I might add, you will *definitely* need to add
the 4d51 module to your Tru64 kernel and rebuild.  If you don't have this
module in your installation, you can find it on the associated product
disk that came with your Tru64 set, or you can download from the links
provided at this site:

>http://moon.hanya-n.org/comp/alpha/hct/graphics.html


if you plan to use NT or Windows 2000 this site has a lot of the drivers,
etc. you will need

ftp://dutlbcz.lr.tudelft.nl/alphant/

good luck

jn

On my pws 500a, i get into alpha bios simply by typing "arc" at the srm
prompt.  That way you don't have to reset your OS type in Alpha Bios -
assuming *nix will be your main operating system.

If you are running a combo of Tru64, VMS and/or Linux the absolute best
video card is the 3Dlabs Oxygen VX1 PCI.


